  "worked_solution": "First, we factor $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ from the first two terms of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{3}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{3}\u2061x+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot 1+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}+{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+{csc}^{2}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{3}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{3}\u2061x+1}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+{csc}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$",
